  "id": "mos-far-memset-wrong-bank",
  "title": "Far memset selects the near runtime and loses the destination bank",
  "status": "fixed",
  "summary": "The June 26 4096-byte fill is causally repaired by existing a81874d / patch 0013. Identical retained IR calls near __memset without the patch (4096 physical bytes wrong, checksum 0) and __memset_far with it (all bytes 0x42, checksum 0x2000). The baseline compiler is explicitly reconstructed; no new compiler fix was needed.",
  "report": "docs/investigations/2026-09-26-far-memset-revalidation.md",
  "attribution": [
    "OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.0 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session 01a0db16-f6a0-7e32-ada6-0c8098813933: reconstruction, revalidation, regression coverage, process enforcement, and documentation. No new executable compiler or runtime change.",
    "Existing a81874d credit is preserved verbatim in historical-commit.txt: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context). Tool version, exact model ID/version from session metadata, and reasoning effort remain unknown; no attribution is guessed."
  ],
  "reproducer_origin": "original",
  "unknowns": "The exact June source is recovered from c75750e9, but the June compiler and crash-era preprocessed TU are unavailable. Current preprocessing is newly generated. The comparison isolates removal of 0013 on the captured September fork; it is not the June toolchain. Closure covers the original 4096-byte fill and near/far runtime routing, not every far memory operation or lengths above 65535.",
